L4-E7: REAL COMPONENT SETTINGS FOR BOARD E'S SOLAR STAGE (layer 4, MESHSAT-1357, 1 October 2026)
prototype design, desk arithmetic; nothing bought, built, powered or measured. Bases: MAKER, NETLIST, CATALOGUE, MODELED,
INFERRED, ASSUMPTION, SESSION, as named on each line

0. REPRODUCTIONS (before any figure)
   0a l4e_replay.py in a child process reproduces l4e_replay.out byte for byte: yes
   0b l4e5_source_control.py in a child process reproduces l4e5_source_control.out byte for byte: yes
   0c l4e_replay.main() in-process, locals captured, prints l4e_replay.out byte for byte: yes
   (the functions used below are the replay's: i_factor, ec_row, pdf_lines, hold, trace, meanday, least; no git hash compared)

1. BOARD E AS DRAWN (NETLIST v2/ecad/pcb-e1-dock-e7/out/pcb-e1-dock.net, pinned)
   - U5 pins 32 (CSNIN), 33 (CSPIN) and 34 (VIN) all on PV_P: the input-current sense is tied off, so as drawn no input limit acts (8705af p.12, p.31)
   - U5 pin 38 (IMON_IN) on TRK_IMONI with R16 alone, 10k, and no CIMON_IN
   - U5 pins 29 to 31 (EXTVCC, CSNOUT, CSPOUT) on TRK_OUT: INTVCC is regulated from the output (8705af p.32)
   - U5's LCSC field C674164 and its land WQFN-38-1EP_5x7mm_P0.5mm_EP3.15x5.15mm
   - R8 102k 1% from PV_P to TRK_FBIN, R9 7.50k 1% to GND
   - R12 215k (RT), the oscillator's 202 kHz row
   - Q3 and Q5 BSC028N06NS (M1, M3), Q4 and Q6 BSC039N06NS (M2, M4)
   - PV_P carries F2, D4, the bulk C11 to C15, C64, Q3's drain, R8, R14, TP5 and U5
   gen_sch_e.py's R10 reads 115k; L4-E5 (its record, reproduced in 0b) raises it to 232k, ceiling 28.28 / 29.21 / 30.15 V

2. THE MAKERS' ROWS USED
   LT8705A 8705af (v2/vendor/power/lt8705a.pdf): p.3 order table: grades in the drawn QFN (UHF): E, I; H and MP only in the
     TSSOP (FE); p.6 Note 3, its U+2013 minus written -:
       "Note 3: The LT8705AE is guaranteed to meet performance specifications from 0°C to 125°C junction temperature.
       Specifications over the -40°C to 125°C operating junction temperature range are assured by design, characterization
       and correlation with statistical process controls. The LT8705AI is guaranteed over the full -40°C to 125°C junction
       temperature range."
   p.4 IMON_IN regulation 1.187 / 1.208 / 1.229 V (full range); line regulation max 0.005 %/V (25 C, VIN 12 to 80 V, not switching);
     p.5 A7 gm E, I 0.94 / 1.06 mmho (full range), all grades 0.95 / 1.05 (25 C); EA2 gain 130 V/V TYP only; p.4 FBIN E, I
     1.184 / 1.205 / 1.226 V (full range); EA3 gain 90 V/V TYP only; p.5 IMON_IN fault 1.55 / 1.61 / 1.67 V; IMON_IN output
     current at least 100 uA; CSPIN-CSNIN differential -100 to 100 mV; p.31 CIMON_IN > 100 / (f x RIMON_IN), 0.1 to 1 uF in a
     current loop; p.2 QFN theta-JA 34 C/W; p.3 VIN quiescent 4.2 mA max; p.6 fOSC at RT 215k up to 235 kHz
   Milliohm HoJLR2512 series (v2/vendor/passives/milliohm-hojlr2512-series.pdf, Ho-A0): p.1 F = +-1 %; p.2 TCR +-50 ppm/K
     (2 to 500 mOhm), 3 W derating from 70 C to 0 at 170 C (33.3 K/W, INFERRED as r11_dep.py); p.4 the TCR test spans +25 to
     +125 C only; soldering heat < +-0.5 %; load life < +-1 %
   YAGEO RT series V.16, May 06 2025 (held: v2/vendor/passives/held/yageo-rt-series-v16-2025-05-06.pdf): p.2 B = +-0.1 %,
     D = 25 ppm/K; p.7 TCR tested at +25/-55 C and +25/+125 C; life +-(0.5 % + 0.05 Ohm); p.8 soldering heat +-(0.5 % + 0.05 Ohm)
   Infineon BSC028N06NS Rev.2.1 p.3 (held) Qg max 49 nC; BSC039N06NS Rev.2.4 p.4 Qg max 32 nC (both VGS 0 to 10 V)
   the envelope (v2/ecad/tools/pcb_envelope.yaml): ambient in use -20 to 40 C (REQ-024, D-02a); worst inside air 62.1 C

3. THE DECISIONS
   GRADE: LT8705AI in the drawn QFN (LT8705AIUHF#PBF, LCSC C674169; #TRPBF C674170), replacing the netlist's C674164
     (LT8705AEUHF#TRPBF, the E grade). The H and MP grades exist only in the TSSOP, which is not the drawn land. Of E and I,
     only I is GUARANTEED (tested) below 0 C junction; the kit starts cold at -20 C ambient, so its junction range starts at
     -20 C. With I fixed, A7's limits are 0.94 / 1.06 mmho (the replay stacked H and MP's 0.93 because no grade was named).
     Hot end (INFERRED): INTVCC from EXTVCC on TRK_OUT up to L4-E5's 30.15 V; gate charge 2 x 49 + 2 x 32 nC at 235 kHz plus
     4.2 mA: 42.3 mA, 1.27 W, TJ at most 105.4 C in 62.1 C air with theta-JA 34 C/W (84.5 C at the drawn output's 15.56 V), under
     125 C.
     So the I grade's tested range, -40 to 125 C junction, covers -20 to 105.4 C. Catalogue: stock 0 at LCSC on 1 October 2026
     (U5 is bench-fitted; another distributor)
   RSENSE1 (new, R59): 15 mOhm, Milliohm HoJLR2512-3W-15mR-1%, LCSC C2903494 (stock 4871): +-1 % (CATALOGUE and MAKER p.1),
     +-50 ppm/K (MAKER p.2). Rule (SESSION): the family value that puts the zero-margin limit (3.607 A) nearest A7's printed
     50 mV test point (p.5), since no A7 offset row is printed; at the chosen setting 52.1 mV
   RIMON_IN (R16): 23.2k, YAGEO RT0603BRD0723K2L, LCSC C861244 (stock 4030): +-0.1 %, +-25 ppm/K (MAKER p.2, CATALOGUE).
     Rule (SESSION): the largest stocked RT0603BRD07 setting whose 25 V corner stays at or under 100 W at both ends with every
     printed limit, the resistors' printed soldering-heat and life drifts stacked, EA2's gain at 1/2 of its typical and the
     line regulation at 2 times its printed maximum. ACHIEVED SETTING: 1.208 V / (1 mmho x 15 mOhm x 23.2k) = 3.4713 A
     candidates (setting A; worst corner at the typical rows / under the floor with drifts, W):
        22.0k C469656   stock  50468  3.6606 A  101.497 / 105.111
        22.1k C723484   stock  27904  3.6440 A  101.038 / 104.635
        22.3k C861235   stock     10  3.6114 A  100.132 / 103.697  (stock under 1000)
        22.6k C861236   stock   9240  3.5634 A   98.803 / 102.320  (zero margin)
        23.2k C861244   stock   4030  3.4713 A   96.247 /  99.674  <- chosen
        23.7k C861245   stock    648  3.3980 A   94.217 /  97.571  (stock under 1000)
        24.0k C326729   stock  59731  3.3556 A   93.039 /  96.351
        24.3k C136968   stock  29267  3.3141 A   91.891 /  95.162
        24.6k C861250   stock   1689  3.2737 A   90.770 /  94.001
        24.9k C136967   stock   6232  3.2343 A   89.676 /  92.869
     CIMON_IN (new, C65): 100n, LCSC C14663: above p.31's minimum 25.4 nF at the slowest oscillator, at the 0.1 uF lower end; tau 2.32 ms
   THE HOLD: R8 94.2k (RT0603BRD0794K2L, LCSC C861602, stock 9520) over R9 7.5k (RT0603BRD077K5L, LCSC C728597, stock 32275), 0.1 %, 25 ppm/K: nominal 16.340 V
     Rule (SESSION): of the 97 stocked pairs with a nominal from 15.5 to 17.5 V, the one whose band's worse end gives the most energy
     on SC-37's day (the model's hourly maximum-power voltage there runs 16.34 to 16.70 V). The best eight (worse end Wh, pair, band):
       370.6 Wh   94.2k / 7.50k  15.763 / 16.340 / 16.921 V
       370.4 Wh  102.0k / 8.20k  15.622 / 16.194 / 16.770 V
       370.3 Wh   91.0k / 7.32k  15.614 / 16.185 / 16.761 V
       370.3 Wh  113.0k / 9.09k  15.613 / 16.185 / 16.760 V
       370.2 Wh  105.0k / 8.45k  15.607 / 16.178 / 16.754 V
       370.1 Wh   90.9k / 7.32k  15.598 / 16.169 / 16.744 V
       370.1 Wh  113.0k / 9.10k  15.597 / 16.168 / 16.743 V
       370.0 Wh   93.1k / 7.50k  15.593 / 16.163 / 16.738 V
     the band (FBIN's I-grade limits, its line term, the FBIN bias, R8 and R9 at 0.1 % and 25 ppm/K at both ends):
       EA3 at its typical 90 V/V: 15.763 / 16.340 / 16.921 V; EA3 at half: 15.538 / 17.148 V; with the resistors' drifts too: 15.253 / 17.470 V
     as drawn the band was 16.695 / 17.593 / 18.490 V (the replay: 1 % parts, H and MP's FBIN minimum)

4. THE 100 W CORNER CHECK ON THE ACHIEVED VALUES (section 11's physics: the replay's i_factor, 8705af p.31)
   envelope: 15.538 V (the hold's lowest, EA3 at half) to REQ-016's 25 V in 0.01 V steps; I grade; both ends:
     the cold end: RSENSE1 at -20.0 C, RIMON_IN at -20.0 C
     the hot end: RSENSE1 at 70.1 C, RIMON_IN at 62.1 C (RSENSE1 0.24 W x 33.3 K/W over the air, INFERRED)
   A. THE CHECK (printed limits; the two TYP-only rows as the replay carries them: EA2 at 130 V/V over VC's absolute range, line at its 25 C maximum):
     the cold end worst 96.2474 W at 25.000 V (ref 1.229 V, line +, gm 0.94, RSENSE1 x0.98777, RIMON_IN x0.99788, EA2 +); margin 3.7526 W; 60736 corners
     the hot end  worst 96.2291 W at 25.000 V (ref 1.229 V, line +, gm 0.94, RSENSE1 x0.98777, RIMON_IN x0.99807, EA2 +); margin 3.7709 W; 60736 corners
   B. printed rows alone (information: EA2's and the line term left out):
     the cold end worst 95.2909 W at 25.000 V (ref 1.229 V, line -, gm 0.94, RSENSE1 x0.98777, RIMON_IN x0.99788, EA2 -); margin 4.7091 W; 60736 corners
     the hot end  worst 95.2727 W at 25.000 V (ref 1.229 V, line -, gm 0.94, RSENSE1 x0.98777, RIMON_IN x0.99807, EA2 -); margin 4.7273 W; 60736 corners
   C. the design floor (EA2 at 65 V/V, line x2, the resistors' soldering and life drifts stacked: SESSION):
     the cold end worst 99.6739 W at 25.000 V (ref 1.229 V, line +, gm 0.94, RSENSE1 x0.97301, RIMON_IN x0.98792, EA2 +); margin 0.3261 W; 60736 corners
     the hot end  worst 99.6549 W at 25.000 V (ref 1.229 V, line +, gm 0.94, RSENSE1 x0.97300, RIMON_IN x0.98811, EA2 +); margin 0.3451 W; 60736 corners
   D. drifts at the typical rows (information):
     the cold end worst 98.6931 W at 25.000 V (ref 1.229 V, line +, gm 0.94, RSENSE1 x0.97301, RIMON_IN x0.98792, EA2 +); margin 1.3069 W; 60736 corners
     the hot end  worst 98.6743 W at 25.000 V (ref 1.229 V, line +, gm 0.94, RSENSE1 x0.97300, RIMON_IN x0.98811, EA2 +); margin 1.3257 W; 60736 corners
   VERDICT: A PASSES at both ends with a margin of 3.75 W, and C (the floor) passes; refused above 100 W
   THE UNPRINTED ROWS, as break-even values for this setting (the corner reaches 100 W at the value shown):
     EA2's gain, line x1                  cold end 25.0 V/V, hot end 24.9 V/V
     EA2's gain, line x1   , with drifts  cold end 53.6 V/V, hot end 53.2 V/V
     EA2's gain, line x2                  cold end 25.4 V/V, hot end 25.3 V/V
     EA2's gain, line x2   , with drifts  cold end 55.2 V/V, hot end 54.7 V/V
     EA2's gain, line x5                  cold end 26.4 V/V, hot end 26.3 V/V
     EA2's gain, line x5   , with drifts  cold end 60.5 V/V, hot end 59.9 V/V
     EA2's gain, line x10                 cold end 28.4 V/V, hot end 28.3 V/V
     EA2's gain, line x10  , with drifts  cold end 72.2 V/V, hot end 71.3 V/V
     the line regulation (cold end) at EA2 130 V/V: up to 61.6 times its printed maximum (0.308 %/V); at 65 V/V: 47.1 times
     RSENSE1's TCR below 25 C (HoJLR prints its TCR from +25 to +125 C only, so the cold end applies it as an ASSUMPTION): the
     cold corner passes up to 882 ppm/K
   for comparison, the replay's 3.548 A on these parts would take 98.375 W at the worse end
   CONDITIONS: sense voltage at the limit's highest 57.5 mV (operating range 100 mV); IMON_IN 60.9 uA at it (at least 100 uA);
     the fault (IMON_IN 1.67 V maximum) at up to 76.7 mV across RSENSE1; the candidate's hot short circuit through RSENSE1 97.4 mV,
     inside the operating range; no resistor in series with CSPIN or CSNIN (p.30): R59's pads are their Kelvin taps

